# What the image build must not take from the working tree.
#
# The Dockerfile's `COPY . .` would otherwise pull in whatever a local checkout
# happens to be carrying, which is a correctness problem and not only a size one.

# Platform-specific by construction (esbuild ships a native binary per os/cpu), so a
# tree installed on the host would be copied into a Linux image and used from there.
# The web stage runs its own `npm ci`.
webui/node_modules

# Built by the web stage. Excluded so the committed copy — which exists only so
# `go build` works without a Node toolchain — can never be what ships. If the stage
# fails to supply it, go:embed fails the build instead of embedding a stale UI.
web/dist

# Build inputs, not source.
.git
.github
autotaggerr
autotaggerr.exe
cover.out

# The developer's own runtime state. config/ holds config.json, the database and the
# artwork cache; copying it in would bake one machine's install into an image.
config
